The Intuit CRM Analytics (CRMA) team plays a vital role in optimizing user journeys and driving growth across the QuickBooks ecosystem. The CRMA team's core mission is to deliver AI/ML-driven, personalized, actionable insights to provide delightful customer experiences and drive ecosystem revenue.

Our LatentView team is embedded within CRMA and owns the analytics engine behind marketing campaigns, experimentation, and product performance across Intuit's Growth Products portfolio — including Payments, Payroll, Capital, Bill Pay, IBCC, and QBO Core. Our services span weekly performance commentary, A/B experiment analysis, wrap reporting, and self-service product analytics dashboards.

🔮Overview about the Project

The CRMA AI Analytics Platform is a suite of interconnected, AI-powered modules that automate the full marketing analytics lifecycle — from weekly narrative generation, to experiment health tracking, to automated readouts, to decision-ready wrap analysis — all unified under a single self-service workbench (the CRMA Hub).

Rather than a single tool, the platform is the analytics backbone for Intuit's Growth Products portfolio. Each product team gets its own experiment registry, automated sanity pipeline, and wrap-analysis workflow, all running on shared infrastructure and accessible from one place.

❗Problem Statement

Intuit's CRMA organization manages marketing campaigns across 30+ product domains. Every week, the team needed to produce leadership commentary, track 100+ live experiments, generate readouts at precise baking milestones, and deliver wrap-up analysis to inform ramp/kill decisions. All of this was manual.

The manual process created recurring pain:

~40 Lifecycle Marketing Managers spending ~2 hours each on weekly commentary.

Analysts pulling experiment data from Excel, computing metrics by hand, and manually publishing HTML dashboards.

Experiment readouts (Day 0 / 2 / 9 / 25 / 40) tracked from memory and spreadsheets — readouts missed, numbers mismatched, feedback lost.

Reporting scaling linearly with business complexity — every new experiment added directly to the workload.

🔧 Approach / Methodology

We designed and delivered the platform in phases over ~3 months, shipping six production modules that each reinforce the others.

Phase 1: Channel Health Commentary Agent (May 2026)

An AI agent generates a weekly 5-section ELM engagement brief from pipeline data. Stakeholders review and comment inline; a second AI agent incorporates feedback automatically. Published to an interactive dashboard and QuickSight for leadership.

Phase 2: AURA Experiments Dashboard (Jun 2026)

An automated pipeline tracks 30+ experiments, computes ITC, classifies each signal (Positive / Mixed / Flat / Negative), and generates AI commentary per experiment — refreshed weekly on zero-infra hosting.

Phase 3: Experiment Auto-Executor (Jun 2026)

Automates the full experiment lifecycle — D0 learning plan, D2 sanity check, and D9/D25/D40 baking readouts — triggered by days-since-launch. Zero missed readouts; scales to 150+ experiments.

Phase 4: AI-Powered Wrap Analysis (Jun 2026)

AI-assisted wrap reports with Bayesian statistical tests, guardrail checks, and cross-validation against source dashboards — delivering decision-ready ramp/kill recommendations to product managers and experiment owners.

Phase 5: Product Analytics Dashboards (ongoing)

Dedicated live analytics dashboards for Payments, Payroll, Capital, IBCC, and Bill Pay — each with an experiment registry, an automated daily sanity pipeline, and weekly business reviews.

Phase 6: CRMA Hub — Unified Analytics Workbench (Jul 2026)

A single self-service front door aggregating every AI output across 30+ product domains, with deep-linkable views, live experiment registries, and embedded reports.

The result is a compounding value loop: Data Pipelines → AI-Generated Insight → Interactive Dashboards → Faster Decisions, with stakeholder feedback flowing back into the AI automatically.





